# [NVIDIA RTX Driver Release 615 R615 (616.92) | Windows 11](https://www.nvidia.com/en-us/drivers/details/279748/)

**NVIDIA RTX Enterprise New Feature Branch Driver**   
  
Release 615 is a New Feature Branch (NFB) release of the NVIDIA RTX Enterprise Driver. NFB drivers provide users the flexibility to try new features made available outside the launch cycle of longer-lived Production Branch drivers. NFB drivers are tested for workstation environments and are recommended for early adopter users who need specific features mentioned in the release highlights or release notes. For the most stable and fully supported enterprise driver, please use the Production Branch graphics driver downloadable from the NVIDIA driver download page.   
  
**Fixed Issues in Version R615 U1**

- Fixed a rare correctness issue on Blackwell GPUs affecting kernels with two or more nested levels of thread divergence, where reconvergence could fail. Kernels with only a single level of divergence are unaffected, as are applications already built with NVCC 13.2.2 or newer. This fix guarantees correct execution, though it may come with a modest performance cost. Recompiling with NVCC 13.2.2 or newer will resolve the possible slowdown. If you are unable to recompile your application for any reason, the runtime behavior of this fix is controllable on a per-process-launch basis through the environment variable   
    
  CUDA\_SELECTIVE\_DEVICE\_CODE\_RECOMPILE as follows:
  - CUDA\_SELECTIVE\_DEVICE\_CODE\_RECOMPILE=DEFAULT
    - Default behavior: attempt JIT recompilation for 15 seconds, runtime patch remaining code
  - CUDA\_SELECTIVE\_DEVICE\_CODE\_RECOMPILE=FORCED
    - Re-finalize every eligible module, ignoring the time budget
  - CUDA\_SELECTIVE\_DEVICE\_CODE\_RECOMPILE=DISABLED
    - Driver patching only, never re-finalize.
- Ongoing bug fixes and enhancements.

If you would like to be notified of upcoming drivers for Windows, please [subscribe here](https://www.nvidia.com/en-us/preferences/email-signup/).

---

## Overview

This package installs the latest Nvidia RTX Driver (Formerly Nvidia Quadro) for Windows 10/11 with the default settings. 
**This package is for RTX / RTX PRO / Quadro cards only.**
You can automate driver updates with `choco upgrade nvidia-rtx-driver -y` in a scheduled task.
You can revert to previous driver versions with `choco install` and specifying the version. i.e. `choco install nvidia-rtx-driver --version=553.62 -yf`

## Package Parameters

The following package parameters can be set to customize the installation.

  - `/SkipCompatCheck` - Skip the compatibility check that ensures your GPU is supported by this driver version. Use at your own risk.
  - `/RemoveOtherVersions` - If desired, remove other versions of the NVIDIA display driver from windows after install.
    - Can trigger an unexpected reboot (uncommon)
    - Removes any nvidia display driver that doesn't match the version of the newly installed version, only affects display driver other components are untouched.
    - Can help prevent windows from reverting to a 'newer' driver on reboot if reverting to an older version of the driver.

Example param usage with choco install command:
`choco install nvidia-rtx-driver --params "'/RemoveOtherVersions'" -yf`

